{
  "note": "Hand-written (phase 4 design, lifecycle 4.4). The test-only note types phase 2's sync tests chart on, in place of the keys they made up before note types existed (vitals, wound_care), with the paths those tests use. Each is a resolved definition as the export writes one; a team holds it with the hash sha256Hex(canonicalJson(definition)). test_note is a Non-Medical note type (offered for both kinds of encounter), so the Medical gate never applies to it; test_medical is a Medical note type with the same sections. No field is required, so a note on either passes the finish check whatever it holds. rows repeats: its entries give a note as many answers as a test needs. more.detail shows only while more.none is not ticked, so an answer there can be one that does not count (lifecycle 4.4, notCounted). redFlags is a Medical note type marked auto: 'medical', as the Red flags and disposition note is (forms 6.2): a visit's finished one lets its Medical notes be finished (lifecycle 4.6, red_flags_first), and its one required answer, flags.any, makes the finish check fail while it is empty (incomplete); the sign-off tests install it in their own team. services/api/test/sync-fixtures.ts installs both noteTypes in every test team; the phone's tests read them through apps/mobile/test/sync/test_note_types.dart. Never installed outside tests.",
